#slide()[
#text(size: 30pt, weight: "bold")[Sunk Cost Fallacy Explained]
#v(40pt)
#only("1-")[🧮 Tendency to continue an endeavor once an investment has been made]
#v(20pt)
#only("2-")[💰 Investment can be money, effort, or time]
#v(20pt)
#only("3-")[🎰 Leads to continuing unprofitable investments]
#v(20pt)
#only("4-")[🎯 Rational decision-making should be based on future costs and benefits, not past investments]

#only("1")[#voiceover("The sunk cost fallacy is the tendency to continue an endeavor once an investment has been made. This is a cognitive bias that affects decision-making.")]
#only("2")[#voiceover("The investment can be in the form of money, effort, or time. People feel committed to the endeavor because of these past investments.")]
#only("3")[#voiceover("This fallacy often leads to continuing unprofitable investments. People keep investing in a project or activity because they've already put so much into it, even if it's no longer rational to do so.")]
#only("4")[#voiceover("However, rational decision-making should be based on future costs and benefits, not past investments. Sunk costs are costs that have already been incurred and cannot be recovered, so they should not influence future decisions.")]
]

#slide()[
#text(size: 30pt, weight: "bold")[Sunk Cost Fallacy Example]
#v(40pt)
#only("1-")[🎟️ Imagine you bought a ticket to a concert for \$100]
#v(20pt)
#only("2-")[🌧️ On the day of the concert, there's a huge storm]
#v(20pt)
#only("3-")[❓ You're considering whether to still go to the concert]
#v(20pt)
#only("4-")[💭 Sunk cost fallacy: "I've already paid \$100, I should go regardless of the storm"]
#v(20pt)
#only("5-")[🧠 Rational thinking: "The \$100 is gone whether I go or not. Is it worth the discomfort and risk to attend in this storm?"]

#only("1")[#voiceover("Let's consider an example to illustrate the sunk cost fallacy. Imagine you bought a ticket to a concert for 100 dollars.")]
#only("2")[#voiceover("On the day of the concert, there's a huge storm. The weather is really unpleasant and it might be dangerous to go out.")]
#only("3")[#voiceover("You're considering whether to still go to the concert given these circumstances.")]
#only("4")[#voiceover("The sunk cost fallacy might lead you to think, 'I've already paid 100 dollars for this ticket, I should go regardless of the storm.'")]
#only("5")[#voiceover("However, rational thinking would suggest, 'The 100 dollars is gone whether I go to the concert or not. The real question is, is it worth the discomfort and risk to attend in this storm?' The sunk cost should not factor into the decision.")]
]

